code: camelCase the lofi.job_* wire surface end-to-end

Snake_case keys had leaked into both directions of the job API: input
args (timeout_ms on job_wait, interval_ms on job_notify) and output
payloads (exit_code, duration_ms, log_path, total_bytes, notify_*
fields). The rest of the sandboxed surface is camelCase (timeoutMs on
bash, timeoutMs on job_spawn), so the jobs family now matches.

Inputs renamed: timeout_ms -> timeoutMs, interval_ms -> intervalMs.
Outputs renamed: exitCode, durationMs, timeoutMs, logPath, totalBytes,
notifyIntervalMs, notifyChanged.

Spawn now accepts the two knobs it used to drop on the floor: notify
silences the job entirely, and notifyIntervalMs turns on periodic
progress ticks without needing a follow-up job_notify call. Passing
the interval implies notify: true.